            "review_text": "chanyu1\ncalifornia653 contributions\n0\nOverrated Seafood Dishes\nNov 2019\nWe were brought here by our tour guide insisting that it is the number one rated seafood restaurant in Halong City and that it is very difficult to get a table during normal dining hours. Somehow, he was able to get us a table during the peak dining hours of 6:30 p.m. that same morning. The place was crowded with diners when we arrived, a good sign. Our tour guide introduced us to a few dishes this restaurant is known for: a soup with a small local fish with local vegetables, live shrimp grilled as well as deep fried, and their famous seafood fried rice. The fish soup was unusual with a little sour, tangy taste to it, and the small fish contains small bones so eating the fish was somewhat laborious. The soup did have some unusual but tasty flavor to it. If the shrimp in the 2 different style of cooking was live before cooking, they destroyed it by overcooking it as the shrimp meat was sticking to the shell when peeled. They either overcooked it or the shrimp was not lively fresh. I'll give them the benefit of the doubt in that it was overcooked. The seafood fried rice, their signature dish, was hard and lacked taste. Very disappointing. So the food is not as good as our tour guide claims and overrated. However, a redeeming factor is that the final price was reasonable considering the location being in a tourist zone. So average seafood at a reasonable price for this place...\nRead more\nValue\nService\nFood\nReview collected in partnership with this restaurant \nWritten November 15, 2019",
